Dual optimization. For sparsity experiments, we consider ν=0
u=0. Since the constraint is deterministic given the state of the model (it does not need to be estimated from mini-batches), we consider the use of an EMA to not be crucial for this task. Unless otherwise stated, we use a dual step-size of 8⋅10−48\cdot 10^{-4} for all dual optimizer choices (as was provided by Gallego-Posada et al. (2022)). We decide against tuning the dual step-size separately for each optimizer to highlight the flexibility of 𝝂 m{
u}PI: given a step-size that was tuned to yield good results for GA, 𝝂 m{
u}PI may produce better-behaved dynamics.
